0..74 Comment "// Tactics over goals: a splice `~t` stands where a value is read and runs"
75..150 Comment "// the tactic `t` at the goal the position holds, the binders in scope with"
151..220 Comment "// their types and the type the value is checked against. The checker"
221..294 Comment "// runs the tactic, judges the term it answers against the goal again and"
295..372 Comment "// fills the splice with it, so the kernel replays the filled declaration and"
373..451 Comment "// no tactic is trusted. Two tactics stand: `assumption`, the innermost binder"
452..527 Comment "// whose type is the goal\'s, and `intro(t)`, a function whose body is `t`\'s"
528..588 Comment "// answer under the binder it introduces. What refuses is in"
589..651 Comment "// `../../pathological/metaprograms/tactics-over-goals.gandr`."
652..654 Comment "//"
655..670 Comment "// - see: #2762"
